      "question": "How does the Government utilize its authority under Section 19(1) of the Customs Act, 1969, to manage existing fiscal notifications?",
      "answer": "The Government exercises its authority under Section 19(1) in the public interest, in consultation with the National Board of Revenue, to either cancel previous SRO notifications or issue amendments to modify existing customs duty exemptions and related fiscal measures, as evidenced by the various SROs issued between 2010 and 2012.",
